1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:05,820
There once was a stonecutter, who wished to be the mightiest thing in the world.

2
00:00:05,900 --> 00:00:08,720
One day, a rich lord passed by.

3
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:12,100
"If only I were him," he sighed.

4
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:14,920
And so he was.

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,220
But the sun beat down, even on lords.

6
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:20,770
"I want to be the sun!"

7
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:24,620
So he became the sun, and scorched the earth,

8
00:00:24,700 --> 00:00:26,920
until a cloud covered him.

9
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:29,320
"Then let me be the cloud!"

10
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:33,690
He rained, and rained, and flooded the land.

11
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:38,320
But one thing did not move.

12
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:40,740
"Let me be the mountain."

13
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:45,840
Now he was mighty. Unmoving.

14
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:49,140
Until he felt something at his feet.

15
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:52,710
A stonecutter.

16
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:57,060
"Let me be myself," he whispered.

17
00:00:58,400 --> 00:01:02,430
Whatever you become, something will seem greater.

18
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:07,500
Peace begins with who you are.
